Testing for expected failure requires the usage of `ERR_PRINT_OFF/ON` macros, because otherwise the test run is going to be polluted with error messages:
```suggestion
	ERR_PRINT_OFF;
	Error e = image.create(Image::Format(), 27, -35, 40, false, img);
	CHECK(e == ERR_CANT_CREATE);
	ERR_PRINT_ON;
```
